     <h1 class="title" title="Gulmarg Hill Station">Gulmarg</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/north-india-hill-stations/gulmarg-hill-station.jpg" title="Gulmarg hill station" alt="Gulmarg hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Gulmarg" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Baramula District, 57 km from Srinagar<br />
<b>Area:</b> 467sq.Kms<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2730m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 20&#176;C to 25&#176;C , Winter 4&#176;C to 8&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b> May - September, November - February</p>     
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Natural beauty, Lake, Kashmir, Srinagar</p>

<p>The hill resort of Gulmarg is located in the <b>Baramulla district</b> of <b>Jammu and Kashmir</b>. In an incredible height of 2730 meters the hill resort has a gently sloping topography. Gulmarg is 57 km south of the capital, Srinagar and is close to the <b>Indo-Pakistan border</b>.</p>
